    |As you walk into the gloomy cave, you pull out the ornate bullseye lantern you found during your foray into the undermountain and light the oil within, illuminating the path ahead. Without it, you reckon you'd have trouble navigating this place.


]Beyond the narrow corridor, the room expands into a large cavern with a forest of stalagmites. Water drips from the stalactite-covered ceiling. The floor is littered with rubble and broken tools. What catches your attention, though, are the numerous captives and the squalid conditions they're kept in.

The prisoners here are either kept locked up within gated alcoves or forced to wear collars around their necks. The ones with collars appear to be in better condition than the others, but each of their chains lead to a metal spike which is driven into the base of a stalagmite.

